d_at":"2026-10-13T16:51:45Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124393","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124393.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124393.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-13T16:51:45Z"},"body":"When a debug export is launched from the editor, GameViewDebugger sends the runtime node selection setup to the debug session. The exported process could then enable NODE_TYPE_2D, causing RuntimeNodeSelect to intercept mouse input and pass it to CanvasItemManipulator. Controls such as sliders were moved by the editor manipulation tools instead of receiving their normal input.\n\nRuntimeNodeSelect now starts in NODE_TYPE_NONE and ignores 2D/3D node selection requests unless the process is embedded in the editor. Embedded Game view keeps the existing node selection and CanvasItem manipulation behavior, while standalone desktop and web exports keep normal game input.\n\nFixes #124312\n\nValidation:\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- All local-related tests have been passed.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_u